{"name":"Indolence","hex":"#a29dad","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indolence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Habitual laziness or sloth.","Lack of pain in a tumour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indolence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laziness","blocks":[{"text":"Laziness is emotional disinclination to activity or exertion despite having the ability to act or to\nexert oneself. It is often used as a pejorative; terms for a person seen to be lazy include \"couch potato\" and \"slacker\". Related concepts include sloth, a Christian sin, abulia, a medical term for reduced motivation, and lethargy, a state of lacking energy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/British_club_scene.jpg/330px-British_club_scene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laziness","wikidata":"Q484"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/British_club_scene.jpg/500px-British_club_scene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/British_club_scene.jpg/1280px-British_club_scene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/British_club_scene.jpg/500px-British_club_scene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scene in club lounge, by Thomas Rowlandson ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritish_club_scene.jpg"}],"sounds":{"indolence":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-indolence.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-indolence.wav/LL-Q1860_%28en